# The shape of app/.env, for reference only. Do NOT create app/.env
# by copying this file: tools/bootstrap.mjs writes the real one.
#
# Since Nov 2026 the lab has no published password. On first run the
# bootstrap generates random per-cluster passwords, stores them in
# tools/.lab-credentials.json (gitignored), and writes app/.env
# (gitignored) with two connection URLs for the non-superuser app
# role `lab_app`, both on 127.0.0.1 port 54399: DATABASE_URL for the
# `lab` database and PROBES_DATABASE_URL for the `probes` database.
# (No sample URL is printed here on purpose: any user:password@host
# string in a tracked file would trip the lab's own secret scan, and
# a placeholder password invites copy-paste mistakes.)
#
# Run order: npm --prefix tools ci && node tools/bootstrap.mjs, then
# the app commands. app/.env is rewritten on every bootstrap run.
